Please identify the sink values for path traversal (CWE-22) according to the following instructions.
- When a variable/expression is used as argument 0 of a `FileOutputStream` constructor call (the file being opened for writing), it is a sink for path traversal.
Example (illustrative only; report values from the program below):
1. Object stream = new FileOutputStream(target);
- Sink name: target, Line number: 1
Negative example: 1. validate();
Answer: an empty string. A helper call is not the specified sink API.
Now I will give you the program. Please list all the names of sinks and the line numbers.The line numbers should indicate the line of the call that consumes the value.
Do not add extra explanations.Just list the pairs of variable/expression and line number line by line.Each line should start with -.If there is no variable as sink, just output an empty string.
Here are several examples:
Example 1:
- Sink name: a, Line number: 2
Example 2:
- Sink name: (prefix + name), Line number: 3
Here is the program:
```
1. protected void extractFile( final File srcF, final File dir, final InputStream compressedInputStream,
2.                                 final String entryName, final Date entryDate, final boolean isDirectory,
3.                                 final Integer mode, String symlinkDestination )
4.         throws IOException, ArchiverException
5.     {
6.         
7.         final File f = FileUtils.resolveFile( dir, entryName );
8. 
9.         try
10.         {
11.             if ( !isOverwrite() && f.exists() && ( f.lastModified() >= entryDate.getTime() ) )
12.             {
13.                 return;
14.             }
15. 
16.             
17.             final File dirF = f.getParentFile();
18.             if ( dirF != null )
19.             {
20.                 dirF.mkdirs();
21.             }
22. 
23.             if ( !StringUtils.isEmpty( symlinkDestination ) )
24.             {
25.                 SymlinkUtils.createSymbolicLink( f, new File( symlinkDestination ) );
26.             }
27.             else if ( isDirectory )
28.             {
29.                 f.mkdirs();
30.             }
31.             else
32.             {
33.                 OutputStream out = null;
34.                 try
35.                 {
36.                     out = new FileOutputStream( f );
37. 
38.                     IOUtil.copy( compressedInputStream, out );
39.                     out.close();
40.                     out = null;
41.                 }
42.                 finally
43.                 {
44.                     IOUtil.close( out );
45.                 }
46.             }
47. 
48.             f.setLastModified( entryDate.getTime() );
49. 
50.             if ( !isIgnorePermissions() && mode != null && !isDirectory )
51.             {
52.                 ArchiveEntryUtils.chmod( f, mode );
53.             }
54.         }
55.         catch ( final FileNotFoundException ex )
56.         {
57.             getLogger().warn( "Unable to expand to file " + f.getPath() );
58.         }
59.     }
